  "query_preview": "..\n\n...Hot, Dry, Breezy conditions lead to Critical Fire Weather\nFriday and Saturday...\n\nFriday and Saturday: As the ridge axis shifts east and weakens,\na zonal flow pattern sets up over region. Winds will increase \nas warm dry conditions continue. Winds will be west with \nsustained speeds in the teens and gusts into the 20 to 30 mph \nrange. Probability for these winds is around 40-70%. The \nstrongest winds are most likely to remain confined to portions \nof central Washington including the east Cascade valleys and the\nWaterville Plateau. Red Flag Warnings have been issued for most\nof the area for breezy westerly winds and low relative humidity\nboth Friday and Saturday. A Fire Weather Watch remains in \neffect for Colville Reservation since it is borderline. If \nwinds/low RH align enough, an upgrade will be warranted. Highs \nwill be in the upper 80s and 90s with humidity in the teens to \nlow 20s. Overnight lows will be in the 50s to low 60s. Minimum \nrelative humidity will reach the 10-25% range with limited \nrecovery overnight.\n\nSunday through Tuesday: Cooler air will filter into the region.\nWinds will remain diurnally driven with the potential for some \nlocally breezy winds through the Cascade gaps. There is still no\ndecent chance of precip expected through at least Tuesday. \nHighs will generally be in the 80s with low in the upper 40s and\n50s. \n\nWednesday and Thursday: High pressure off the coast will bring \na northwest flow pattern to the region. There is more \nuncertainty in the forecast Wednesday and beyond since some \nensemble members are showing increasing heights, while others \nbring a deeper PacNW trough. A will pas through Southern BC and \nbring about chance for precip across Northeast WA and North ID \nPanhandle. Precip probabilities remain low. /JDC",
